{"geek":{"id":"29b593af-3014-47b2-96fe-cf07264143d6","word":"geek","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"expert in a technical field, particularly to do with computers","tags":["feminine","masculine"],"word":"geek"}],"pos":"noun","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"I once saw a geek bite the head off a live chicken.","bold_text_offsets":[[13,17]],"type":"example","id":"c04a2cb1-2e92-47e1-96d2-2140b1a7af04"},{"text":"You hand in your ticket / And you go watch the geek / Who immediately walks up to you / When he hears you speak / And says, “How does it feel to / be such a freak?”","ref":"1965, Bob Dylan, “Ballad of a Thin Man”, in Highway 61 Revisited:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[47,51]],"id":"8a4ca34f-0926-424a-88c2-aad7e6d37481"}],"categories":["English dated terms","English terms with quotations","English terms with usage examples"],"links":[["performer","performer"]],"raw_glosses":["(dated) A carnival performer specializing in bizarre and unappetizing behavior."],"glosses":["A carnival performer specializing in bizarre and unappetizing behavior."],"tags":["dated"],"id":"c2475f00-7f52-4d8a-acc0-6f0f3c127a43"},{"examples":[{"text":"I was a complete computer geek in high school, but I get out a lot more now.","bold_text_offsets":[[26,30]],"type":"example","id":"bf193de5-5c2f-4c76-8f08-df7cec66040a"},{"text":"Most famous actors are really theater geeks at heart.","bold_text_offsets":[[38,43]],"type":"example","id":"d199096c-a2ba-4448-86ed-58ad92c75687"}],"categories":["English colloquialisms","English terms with usage examples"],"links":[["person","person"],["field","field"],["hobby","hobby"],["attributive noun","attributive noun"]],"synonyms":[{"word":"buff"},{"word":"freak"}],"raw_glosses":["(colloquial) A person who is intensely interested in a particular field or hobby and often having limited or nonstandard social skills. Often used with an attributive noun."],"glosses":["A person who is intensely interested in 