,{"text":"He turned out to be a proper geezer who was willing to listen to my proposition that if he took the door at the Ministry, I would pay him £400 a month to mark my cards.","ref":"2003, Carlton Leach, Muscle, John Blake Publishing, →ISBN:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[29,35]],"id":"40f565a8-b321-4ac7-af84-c01f62d4b9f3"},{"text":"He was a bit of a geezer. Used to box with the Krays when he was a young 'un.","ref":"2009, Dreda Say Mitchell, Geezer Girls, Hachette UK, →ISBN:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[18,24]],"id":"1b09d19b-e9fb-4104-9b8c-64aa9f3173df"},{"text":"When I'd first met Adam, at work when we were both 23, the fact that he seemed a little rough around the edges appealed to me. He was a bit of a geezer, a joker, one of the lads.","ref":"2013, Charlotte Ward, Why Am I Always the One Before 'The One'?, Hachette UK, →ISBN:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[145,151]],"id":"721ba022-963c-44ed-b6de-42e1c8e4928c"}],"categories":["British English","Cockney English","Commonwealth English","English slang","English terms with quotations","Irish English"],"links":[["affable","affable"],["morally","morally"],["dubious","dubious"],["wide boy","wide boy"]],"synonyms":[{"word":"spiv"},{"word":"wide boy"}],"coordinate_terms":[{"word":"chav"}],"raw_glosses":["(UK, Ireland, Commonwealth, chiefly Cockney, slang) Someone affable but morally dubious; a wide boy."],"glosses":["Someone affable but morally dubious; a wide boy."],"tags":["Cockney","Commonwealth","Ireland","UK","slang"],"id":"621e8d20-312d-4be5-9c4a-ebb754573793"},{"examples":[{"text":"Hi, geezer, you alright?","bold_text_offsets":[[4,10]],"type":"example","id":"337525ae-5d1c-4199-87ab-2df9ddd937b4"}],"categories":["British English","Commonwealth English","English slang","English terms with usage examples","Irish English"],"links":[["male","male#English"]],"synonyms":[{"word":"mate"},{"word":"babber","source":"Thesaurus:friend","tags":["UK"]},{"word":"billy","source":"Thesaurus: